course: dictionary
lesson: 7743
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Read the words around the word and ask what the sentence is about. «Pumpkin» can mean a vegetable, the food made from it, or a loving name for a child.
explain: Look at «Mia spent the afternoon carving a pumpkin for Halloween.» The words carving and Halloween point to the orange vegetable. Now look at «Dad made pumpkin soup for tea.» Here pumpkin is the food. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it fits.
explain: «Goodnight, my little pumpkin», said Gran. No vegetable is being carved and no soup is being made. The word little and the warm goodnight are the clues that pumpkin is a loving name for a child.
fact: Pumpkin has three meanings: a vegetable, the food made from it, and a loving name for a child.
fact: A pumpkin is really a fruit, because a botanist calls the part of a plant that holds the seeds a fruit.
fact: Farmers breed giant pumpkins of over 1,000 kilograms, and the record is over 1,200 kilograms.
fact: Pumpkins are carved into jack-o'-lanterns for Halloween, and in the USA and Canada pumpkin pie is eaten at Thanksgiving.
exercise: «Mia spent the afternoon carving a pumpkin for Halloween.» What kind of pumpkin is this? | A bowl of soup | *A large orange vegetable | A kind of hat | A loving name for a child
exercise: «Dad made pumpkin soup for tea.» In this sentence, what is pumpkin? | A stone | A pet name | *The food made from the vegetable | A seed
exercise: «Goodnight, my little pumpkin», said Gran. What does pumpkin mean here? | A seed for planting | A large round vegetable | Pumpkin soup | *A loving name for a child
test: Which sentence uses pumpkin to mean a food? | «The pumpkin sat on the step.» | «The pumpkin had many seeds inside.» | «Goodnight, my little pumpkin.» | *«We had pumpkin pie at Thanksgiving.»
test: Why does a botanist call a pumpkin a fruit? | It grows on a tree | It is sweet and tastes of sugar | *It is the part of the plant that holds the seeds | It is orange and round
exam: «Farmers breed giant pumpkins of over 1,000 kilograms.» What does giant show about the pumpkins? | Very small and light | Orange and round | Soft and sweet | *Very big and heavy
